{"sha": "f61dac0226c62538057844e6304fb6c9631b9026", "filename": "ChangeLog", "status": "modified", "additions": 10, "deletions": 0, "changes": 10, "blob_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libmatroska/blob/0a2d3e3644a7453b6513db2f9bc270f77943573f/ChangeLog", "raw_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libmatroska/raw/0a2d3e3644a7453b6513db2f9bc270f77943573f/ChangeLog", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Matroska-Org/libmatroska/contents/ChangeLog?ref=0a2d3e3644a7453b6513db2f9bc270f77943573f", "patch": "@@ -1,3 +1,13 @@
+2015-10-20  Moritz Bunkus  <moritz@bunkus.org>
+
+        * KaxInternalBlock::ReadData(): Fixed an invalid memory
+        access. When reading a block group or a simple block that uses
+        EBML lacing the frame sizes indicated in the lacing weren't
+        checked against the available number of bytes. If the indicated
+        frame size was bigger than the whole block's size the parser would
+        read beyond the end of the buffer resulting in a heap information
+        leak.
+
 2015-10-17  Moritz Bunkus  <moritz@bunkus.org>

         * Released v1.4.3."}<_**next**_>{"sha": "22d213283603fe51ef85030c6f376468cdaa0537", "filename": "src/KaxBlock.cpp", "status": "modified", "additions": 4, "deletions": 0, "changes": 4, "blob_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libmatroska/blob/0a2d3e3644a7453b6513db2f9bc270f77943573f/src/KaxBlock.cpp", "raw_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libmatroska/raw/0a2d3e3644a7453b6513db2f9bc270f77943573f/src/KaxBlock.cpp", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Matroska-Org/libmatroska/contents/src/KaxBlock.cpp?ref=0a2d3e3644a7453b6513db2f9bc270f77943573f", "patch": "@@ -529,6 +529,8 @@ filepos_t KaxInternalBlock::ReadData(IOCallback & input, ScopeMode ReadFully)
           case LACING_EBML:
             SizeRead = LastBufferSize;
             FrameSize = ReadCodedSizeValue(BufferStart + Mem.GetPosition(), SizeRead, SizeUnknown);
+            if (!FrameSize || (static_cast<uint32>(FrameSize + SizeRead) > LastBufferSize))
+              throw SafeReadIOCallback::EndOfStreamX(SizeRead);
             SizeList[0] = FrameSize;
             Mem.Skip(SizeRead);
             LastBufferSize -= FrameSize + SizeRead;
@@ -537,6 +539,8 @@ filepos_t KaxInternalBlock::ReadData(IOCallback & input, ScopeMode ReadFully)
               // get the size of the frame
               SizeRead = LastBufferSize;
               FrameSize += ReadCodedSizeSignedValue(BufferStart + Mem.GetPosition(), SizeRead, SizeUnknown);
+              if (!FrameSize || (static_cast<uint32>(FrameSize + SizeRead) > LastBufferSize))
+                throw SafeReadIOCallback::EndOfStreamX(SizeRead);
               SizeList[Index] = FrameSize;
               Mem.Skip(SizeRead);
               LastBufferSize -= FrameSize + SizeRead;"}

{"sha": "3fb53d4011fe845f5811c42a8403097b1c99f266", "filename": "ChangeLog", "status": "modified", "additions": 6, "deletions": 0, "changes": 6, "blob_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/blob/24e5cd7c666b1ddd85619d60486db0a5481c1b90/ChangeLog", "raw_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/raw/24e5cd7c666b1ddd85619d60486db0a5481c1b90/ChangeLog", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Matroska-Org/libebml/contents/ChangeLog?ref=24e5cd7c666b1ddd85619d60486db0a5481c1b90", "patch": "@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@
 2015-10-20  Moritz Bunkus  <moritz@bunkus.org>

+        * EbmlElement::ReadCodedSizeValue(): Fixed an invalid memory
+        access. When reading a EBML variable length integer value a read
+        access beyond the end of the available buffer was possible if
+        fewer bytes were available than indicated by the first byte
+        resulting in a heap information leak.
+
         * EbmlUnicodeString::UpdateFromUTF8(): Fixed an invalid memory
         access. When reading from a UTF-8 string in which the length
         indicated by a UTF-8 character's first byte exceeds the string's"}<_**next**_>{"sha": "d25abe83b242ebc016d723f7477b2d2dc544b812", "filename": "src/EbmlElement.cpp", "status": "modified", "additions": 5, "deletions": 0, "changes": 5, "blob_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/blob/24e5cd7c666b1ddd85619d60486db0a5481c1b90/src/EbmlElement.cpp", "raw_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/raw/24e5cd7c666b1ddd85619d60486db0a5481c1b90/src/EbmlElement.cpp", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Matroska-Org/libebml/contents/src/EbmlElement.cpp?ref=24e5cd7c666b1ddd85619d60486db0a5481c1b90", "patch": "@@ -150,6 +150,11 @@ uint64 ReadCodedSizeValue(const binary * InBuffer, uint32 & BufferSize, uint64 &
       // ID found
       PossibleSizeLength = SizeIdx + 1;
       SizeBitMask >>= SizeIdx;
+
+      // Guard against invalid memory accesses with incomplete IDs.
+      if (PossibleSizeLength > BufferSize)
+        break;
+
       for (SizeIdx = 0; SizeIdx < PossibleSizeLength; SizeIdx++) {
         PossibleSize[SizeIdx] = InBuffer[SizeIdx];
       }"}

{"sha": "a5139c4309eb3b5224fd6505c8f973ad6835fd9d", "filename": "ChangeLog", "status": "modified", "additions": 9, "deletions": 0, "changes": 9, "blob_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/blob/ababb64e0c792ad2a314245233db0833ba12036b/ChangeLog", "raw_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/raw/ababb64e0c792ad2a314245233db0833ba12036b/ChangeLog", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Matroska-Org/libebml/contents/ChangeLog?ref=ababb64e0c792ad2a314245233db0833ba12036b", "patch": "@@ -1,3 +1,12 @@
+2015-10-20  Moritz Bunkus  <moritz@bunkus.org>
+
+        * EbmlUnicodeString::UpdateFromUTF8(): Fixed an invalid memory
+        access. When reading from a UTF-8 string in which the length
+        indicated by a UTF-8 character's first byte exceeds the string's
+        actual number of bytes the parser would access beyond the end of
+        the string resulting in a heap information leak. Fixes the issue
+        reported as Cisco TALOS-CAN-0036.
+
 2015-10-17  Moritz Bunkus  <moritz@bunkus.org>

         * Released v1.3.2."}<_**next**_>{"sha": "7b7cd8e97210a7fc82d5da2d9fa4608c143386cf", "filename": "src/EbmlUnicodeString.cpp", "status": "modified", "additions": 38, "deletions": 23, "changes": 61, "blob_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/blob/ababb64e0c792ad2a314245233db0833ba12036b/src/EbmlUnicodeString.cpp", "raw_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/raw/ababb64e0c792ad2a314245233db0833ba12036b/src/EbmlUnicodeString.cpp", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Matroska-Org/libebml/contents/src/EbmlUnicodeString.cpp?ref=ababb64e0c792ad2a314245233db0833ba12036b", "patch": "@@ -47,6 +47,21 @@ START_LIBEBML_NAMESPACE

 // ===================== UTFstring class ===================

+static unsigned int UTFCharLength(uint8 lead)
+{
+  if (lead < 0x80)
+    return 1;
+  else if ((lead >> 5) == 0x6)
+    return 2;
+  else if ((lead >> 4) == 0xe)
+    return 3;
+  else if ((lead >> 3) == 0x1e)
+    return 4;
+  else
+    // Invalid size?
+    return 0;
+}
+
 UTFstring::UTFstring()
   :_Length(0)
   ,_Data(NULL)
@@ -143,39 +158,39 @@ void UTFstring::UpdateFromUTF8()
   delete [] _Data;
   // find the size of the final UCS-2 string
   size_t i;
-  for (_Length=0, i=0; i<UTF8string.length(); _Length++) {
-    uint8 lead = static_cast<uint8>(UTF8string[i]);
-    if (lead < 0x80)
-      i++;
-    else if ((lead >> 5) == 0x6)
-      i += 2;
-    else if ((lead >> 4) == 0xe)
-      i += 3;
-    else if ((lead >> 3) == 0x1e)
-      i += 4;
+  const size_t SrcLength = UTF8string.length();
+  for (_Length=0, i=0; i<SrcLength; _Length++) {
+    const unsigned int CharLength = UTFCharLength(static_cast<uint8>(UTF8string[i]));
+    if ((CharLength >= 1) && (CharLength <= 4))
+      i += CharLength;
     else
       // Invalid size?
       break;
   }
   _Data = new wchar_t[_Length+1];
   size_t j;
-  for (j=0, i=0; i<UTF8string.length(); j++) {
-    uint8 lead = static_cast<uint8>(UTF8string[i]);
-    if (lead < 0x80) {
+  for (j=0, i=0; i<SrcLength; j++) {
+    const uint8 lead              = static_cast<uint8>(UTF8string[i]);
+    const unsigned int CharLength = UTFCharLength(lead);
+    if ((CharLength < 1) || (CharLength > 4))
+      // Invalid char?
+      break;
+
+    if ((i + CharLength) > SrcLength)
+      // Guard against invalid memory access beyond the end of the
+      // source buffer.
+      break;
+
+    if (CharLength == 1)
       _Data[j] = lead;
-      i++;
-    } else if ((lead >> 5) == 0x6) {
+    else if (CharLength == 2)
       _Data[j] = ((lead & 0x1F) << 6) + (UTF8string[i+1] & 0x3F);
-      i += 2;
-    } else if ((lead >> 4) == 0xe) {
+    else if (CharLength == 3)
       _Data[j] = ((lead & 0x0F) << 12) + ((UTF8string[i+1] & 0x3F) << 6) + (UTF8string[i+2] & 0x3F);
-      i += 3;
-    } else if ((lead >> 3) == 0x1e) {
+    else if (CharLength == 4)
       _Data[j] = ((lead & 0x07) << 18) + ((UTF8string[i+1] & 0x3F) << 12) + ((UTF8string[i+2] & 0x3F) << 6) + (UTF8string[i+3] & 0x3F);
-      i += 4;
-    } else
-      // Invalid char?
-      break;
+
+    i += CharLength;
   }
   _Data[j] = 0;
 }"}

{"sha": "154d3d99eb814454a254ad58923d1d0804b0b3db", "filename": "ChangeLog", "status": "modified", "additions": 8, "deletions": 0, "changes": 8, "blob_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/blob/88409e2a94dd3b40ff81d08bf6d92f486d036b24/ChangeLog", "raw_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/raw/88409e2a94dd3b40ff81d08bf6d92f486d036b24/ChangeLog", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Matroska-Org/libebml/contents/ChangeLog?ref=88409e2a94dd3b40ff81d08bf6d92f486d036b24", "patch": "@@ -1,5 +1,13 @@
 2015-10-20  Moritz Bunkus  <moritz@bunkus.org>

+        * EbmlMaster::Read(): When the parser encountered a deeply nested
+        element with an infinite size then a following element of an upper
+        level was not propagated correctly. Instead the element with the
+        infinite size was added into the EBML element tree a second time
+        resulting in memory access after freeing it and multiple attempts
+        to free the same memory address during destruction. Fixes the
+        issue reported as Cisco TALOS-CAN-0037.
+
         * EbmlElement::ReadCodedSizeValue(): Fixed an invalid memory
         access. When reading a EBML variable length integer value a read
         access beyond the end of the available buffer was possible if"}<_**next**_>{"sha": "8537ac3bb609a2d5881de5226276aee980f87b48", "filename": "src/EbmlMaster.cpp", "status": "modified", "additions": 8, "deletions": 0, "changes": 8, "blob_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/blob/88409e2a94dd3b40ff81d08bf6d92f486d036b24/src/EbmlMaster.cpp", "raw_url": "https://github.com/Matroska-Org/libebml/raw/88409e2a94dd3b40ff81d08bf6d92f486d036b24/src/EbmlMaster.cpp", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Matroska-Org/libebml/contents/src/EbmlMaster.cpp?ref=88409e2a94dd3b40ff81d08bf6d92f486d036b24", "patch": "@@ -454,6 +454,14 @@ void EbmlMaster::Read(EbmlStream & inDataStream, const EbmlSemanticContext & sCo
         } else {
           if (DeleteElement)
             delete ElementLevelA;
+
+          if (UpperEltFound) {
+            --UpperEltFound;
+            if (UpperEltFound > 0 || MaxSizeToRead <= 0)
+              goto processCrc;
+            ElementLevelA = FoundElt;
+          }
+
           break;
         }
       }"}

