{"sha": "04926a38383c8cabc56e6e6e14481f2d50fdd368", "filename": "ChangeLog", "status": "modified", "additions": 6, "deletions": 0, "changes": 6, "blob_url": "https://github.com/vadz/libtiff/blob/b18012dae552f85dcc5c57d3bf4e997a15b1cc1c/ChangeLog", "raw_url": "https://github.com/vadz/libtiff/raw/b18012dae552f85dcc5c57d3bf4e997a15b1cc1c/ChangeLog", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vadz/libtiff/contents/ChangeLog?ref=b18012dae552f85dcc5c57d3bf4e997a15b1cc1c", "patch": "@@ -1,3 +1,9 @@
+2015-12-27  Even Rouault <even.rouault at spatialys.com>
+
+	* libtiff/tif_next.c: fix potential out-of-bound write in NeXTDecode()
+	triggered by http://lcamtuf.coredump.cx/afl/vulns/libtiff5.tif
+	(bugzilla #2508)
+
 2015-12-27  Even Rouault <even.rouault at spatialys.com>

 	* libtiff/tif_luv.c: fix potential out-of-bound writes in decode"}<_**next**_>{"sha": "0a5b6352b0d19c7d9719d112d6706080eb4f09a6", "filename": "libtiff/tif_next.c", "status": "modified", "additions": 8, "deletions": 2, "changes": 10, "blob_url": "https://github.com/vadz/libtiff/blob/b18012dae552f85dcc5c57d3bf4e997a15b1cc1c/libtiff/tif_next.c", "raw_url": "https://github.com/vadz/libtiff/raw/b18012dae552f85dcc5c57d3bf4e997a15b1cc1c/libtiff/tif_next.c", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vadz/libtiff/contents/libtiff/tif_next.c?ref=b18012dae552f85dcc5c57d3bf4e997a15b1cc1c", "patch": "@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 	case 0:	op[0]  = (unsigned char) ((v) << 6); break;	\
 	case 1:	op[0] |= (v) << 4; break;	\
 	case 2:	op[0] |= (v) << 2; break;	\
-	case 3:	*op++ |= (v);	   break;	\
+	case 3:	*op++ |= (v);	   op_offset++; break;	\
 	}					\
 }

@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@ NeXTDecode(TIFF* tif, uint8* buf, tmsize_t occ, uint16 s)
 			uint32 imagewidth = tif->tif_dir.td_imagewidth;
             if( isTiled(tif) )
                 imagewidth = tif->tif_dir.td_tilewidth;
+            tmsize_t op_offset = 0;

 			/*
 			 * The scanline is composed of a sequence of constant
@@ -122,10 +123,15 @@ NeXTDecode(TIFF* tif, uint8* buf, tmsize_t occ, uint16 s)
 				 * bounds, potentially resulting in a security
 				 * issue.
 				 */
-				while (n-- > 0 && npixels < imagewidth)
+				while (n-- > 0 && npixels < imagewidth && op_offset < scanline)
 					SETPIXEL(op, grey);
 				if (npixels >= imagewidth)
 					break;
+                if (op_offset >= scanline ) {
+                    TIFFErrorExt(tif->tif_clientdata, module, "Invalid data for scanline %ld",
+                        (long) tif->tif_row);
+                    return (0);
+                }
 				if (cc == 0)
 					goto bad;
 				n = *bp++, cc--;"}

