{"sha": "151c279f649576c214034f37cd5f714dcf07a098", "filename": "doc/security.rst", "status": "modified", "additions": 10, "deletions": 1, "changes": 11, "blob_url": "https://github.com/randombit/botan/blob/987ad747db6d0d7e36f840398f3cf02e2fbfd90f/doc/security.rst", "raw_url": "https://github.com/randombit/botan/raw/987ad747db6d0d7e36f840398f3cf02e2fbfd90f/doc/security.rst", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/randombit/botan/contents/doc/security.rst?ref=987ad747db6d0d7e36f840398f3cf02e2fbfd90f", "patch": "@@ -21,7 +21,16 @@ Advisories
 2016
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

-* 2016-10-8871 (CVE-2016-8871) OAEP side channel
+* 2016-11-27 (CVE-2016-xxxx) Integer overflow in BER decoder
+
+  While decoding BER length fields, an integer overflow could occur. This could
+  occur while parsing untrusted inputs such as X.509 certificates. The overflow
+  does not seem to lead to any obviously exploitable condition, but exploitation
+  cannot be positively ruled out. Only 32-bit platforms are likely affected; to
+  cause an overflow on 64-bit the parsed data would have to be many gigabytes.
+  Bug found by Falko Strenzke, cryptosource GmbH.
+
+* 2016-10-26 (CVE-2016-8871) OAEP side channel

   A side channel in OAEP decoding could be used to distinguish RSA ciphertexts
   that did or did not have a leading 0 byte. For an attacker capable of"}<_**next**_>{"sha": "81c04aa6adfc121aa62733b046d91c8e666a8e03", "filename": "src/lib/asn1/ber_dec.cpp", "status": "modified", "additions": 4, "deletions": 1, "changes": 5, "blob_url": "https://github.com/randombit/botan/blob/987ad747db6d0d7e36f840398f3cf02e2fbfd90f/src/lib/asn1/ber_dec.cpp", "raw_url": "https://github.com/randombit/botan/raw/987ad747db6d0d7e36f840398f3cf02e2fbfd90f/src/lib/asn1/ber_dec.cpp", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/randombit/botan/contents/src/lib/asn1/ber_dec.cpp?ref=987ad747db6d0d7e36f840398f3cf02e2fbfd90f", "patch": "@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
