{"sha": "c4159add31ed8dc2038480c9dd3fc8c8fa8579c8", "filename": "third_party/WebKit/Source/WebCore/ChangeLog", "status": "modified", "additions": 18, "deletions": 0, "changes": 18, "blob_url": "https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/2156ea103b778a64228413a5bf304e18b741a2f6/third_party/WebKit/Source/WebCore/ChangeLog", "raw_url": "https://github.com/chromium/chromium/raw/2156ea103b778a64228413a5bf304e18b741a2f6/third_party/WebKit/Source/WebCore/ChangeLog", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/chromium/chromium/contents/third_party/WebKit/Source/WebCore/ChangeLog?ref=2156ea103b778a64228413a5bf304e18b741a2f6", "patch": "@@ -1,3 +1,21 @@
+2012-12-10  Michael Brüning  <michael.bruning@digia.com>
+
+        [Qt] Builds for Mac are tied to the OS system instead of the SDK version.
+        https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=104529
+
+        Reviewed by Simon Hausmann.
+
+        Using work by Eike Ziller <eike.ziller@digia.com>.
+
+        The build system now first tries to assign the correct system libraries
+        for the SDK being used for Mac builds. If this does not yield any
+        result, it falls back to using the Mac OS version to determine the
+        correct library.
+
+        No new tests (not applicable).
+
+        * WebCore.pri:
+
 2012-12-10  Ilya Tikhonovsky  <loislo@chromium.org>

         Unreviewed: touch RenderingAllInOne.cpp to fix Apple Windows builder."}<_**next**_>{"sha": "d80c987a9aa1733a4a785b8d2ef67fccc3e5f430", "filename": "third_party/WebKit/Source/WebCore/WebCore.pri", "status": "modified", "additions": 16, "deletions": 9, "changes": 25, "blob_url": "https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/2156ea103b778a64228413a5bf304e18b741a2f6/third_party/WebKit/Source/WebCore/WebCore.pri", "raw_url": "https://github.com/chromium/chromium/raw/2156ea103b778a64228413a5bf304e18b741a2f6/third_party/WebKit/Source/WebCore/WebCore.pri", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/chromium/chromium/contents/third_party/WebKit/Source/WebCore/WebCore.pri?ref=2156ea103b778a64228413a5bf304e18b741a2f6", "patch": "@@ -177,18 +177,25 @@ enable?(VIDEO) {
